 remain reconstructed. Modern references bound feature arrangement, not 1904 testimony. See docs/RESEARCH/glessner-west-wing-alcove/work.md and LIBERTIES L331. T-1833 supersedes the T-1830 reconstructed south hip and asymmetric rear eaves following the owner's 2026-10-01 south-gable sketch and two model screenshots. The south end is a solid centered gable, ridge W143.5 at 38.6 ft ng and equal 26.5-ft shoulders. The ridge stays at the north gable height while moving 2.5 ft in plan between S14.6 and S26.83 to preserve the north door/loft axis and center the rear gable. The rear eaves share the north-court roof's 5.7-ft, 26.6-degree kick. These shapes/heights are owner-directed reconstructions, not an attested south elevation; the HABS footprint and window positions remain unchanged. The raised rear roof carries the existing west dormer 7 ft higher (eave 33, apex 37 ft ng) to keep its sash and tile cheeks clear of the host roof; its footprint and hood proportions stay fixed. The courtyard overhang matches the north range at 0.20 m."
